    "result_text": "There's a single test class in the suite, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome notification on successful owner create.\n\n- **New function class** `NotifyWelcome.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 obtains a logger named `NOTIFY` via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")` and emits `Welcome owner: id={} memberId={}` with the owner id and memberId. Modeled on the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step.\n- **Wired into `owners.POST.yml`** as a new `notifyWelcome` step inserted after `audit` (so after `save`, where the generated id is populated) and before `warn`, with the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe test suite is green: `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes (BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0). The captured log confirms the line: `NOTIFY - Welcome owner: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
